---Defines an automated backup policy for a table
---@class gcp.bigtableadmin_v2.AutomatedBackupPolicy
---@field keepHotDuration? string Optional. The amount of time that the automated backups remain hot. If specified, the backups created by this policy are `HOT` backups. If not specified, the backups are `STANDARD` backups. The value must be at least 24 hours and at most 10 days, and can't exceed the policy's `retention_period`. Only SSD instances support `HOT` automated backups.
---@field disabled? boolean Optional. If `true`, automated backups are explicitly disabled on this table. This allows users to opt out of default enablement.
---@field retentionPeriod? string Required. How long the automated backups should be retained. Values must be at least 3 days and at most 90 days.
---@field locations? gcp.bigtableadmin_v2.StringList Optional. A list of Cloud Bigtable zones where automated backups are allowed to be created. If empty, automated backups will be created in all zones of the instance. Locations are in the format `projects/{project}/locations/{zone}`. You can set this field only for tables in Enterprise Plus instances.
---@field frequency? string How frequently automated backups should occur. The only supported value at this time is 24 hours. An undefined frequency is treated as 24 hours.

