---@field logicalDataHddBytes? string Output only. The logical data bytes of the column family stored on HDD.
---@field logicalDataBytes? string How much space the data in the column family occupies. This is roughly how many bytes would be needed to read the contents of the entire column family (e.g. by streaming all contents out).
---@field averageCellsPerColumn? number How many cells are present per column qualifier in this column family, averaged over all rows containing any column in the column family. e.g. For column family "family" in a table with 3 rows: * A row with 3 cells in "family:col" and 1 cell in "other:col" (3 cells / 1 column in "family") * A row with 1 cell in "family:col", 7 cells in "family:other_col", and 7 cells in "other:data" (8 cells / 2 columns in "family") * A row with 3 cells in "other:col" (0 columns in "family", "family" not present) would report (3 + 8 + 0)/(1 + 2 + 0) = 3.66 in this field.

